unit is the number of products ordered in order_date.

Write a solution to get the names of products that have at least 100 units ordered in February 2020 and their amount.
Return the result table in any order.
using CTE: create sold_unit with 2 column: product_id, total_units
using to_char: filter February 2020

| product_id | total_units |
| ---------- | ----------- |
| 1          | 130         |
| 2          | 80          |
| 3          | 5           |
| 5          | 100         |

-- Write your PostgreSQL query statement below
with sold_unit as (
select product_id, sum(unit) as total_units
from Orders
where to_char(order_date, 'YYYY-MM') = '2020-02'
group by product_id 
)
select p.product_name, su.total_units as unit
from Products p 
join sold_unit su on p.product_id = su.product_id
where su.total_units >= 100